<div class="poster-title">
<h2>
            TYPES OF WATER
            <span>USED IN RESTAURANT</span>
</h2>
<div class="sub">Different Water, Different Purpose!</div>
</div>

<div class="poster-card">
<h3>1. STILL WATER</h3>
<ul><li>No carbonation</li><li>Plain and natural</li><li>Most commonly served with meals</li></ul>
</div>
<div class="poster-card">
<h3>2. SPARKLING WATER</h3>
<ul><li>Contains carbon dioxide (CO₂)</li><li>Fizzy and refreshing</li><li>Often served with fine dining meals</li></ul>
</div>
<div class="poster-card">
<h3>3. NATURAL MINERAL WATER</h3>
<ul><li>From natural underground sources</li><li>Contains minerals like calcium, magnesium, etc.</li><li>No artificial minerals added</li></ul>
<div class="example evian">evian</div>
</div>
<div class="poster-card">
<h3>4. PURIFIED WATER</h3>
<ul><li>Treated through processes like RO, UV, distillation</li><li>Free from impurities</li><li>Safe for drinking</li></ul>
</div>
<div class="poster-card">
<h3>5. SPRING WATER</h3>
<ul><li>Comes directly from natural springs</li><li>Naturally filtered through rocks</li><li>Fresh and clean taste</li></ul>
<div class="example">SPRING WATER</div>
</div>
<div class="poster-card">
<h3>6. FLAVOURED WATER</h3>
<ul><li>Water infused with fruits, herbs or natural flavors</li><li>Refreshing and healthy option</li></ul>
<div class="flavors">🍋 Lemon · 🌿 Mint · 🥒 Cucumber · 🍓 Berry</div>
</div>

